            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lostangel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "i made an 8X8 pan cuz i didnt have a big enough bag of fritos. Super easy to make, and they taste awesome! The pan i made was gone in 5 minutes! Will be sharing this recipe n definately making again :)"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Patty2007"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Was really good! I went the old fashioned way and used regular marshmallows instead of marshmallow crème. Went together just as easily as Rice Krispie treats. I could easily eat an entire pan of these, but man-o-man the calorie count has to be enormous on these! Sure would be a fun way to eat an entire bag of Fritos though :)",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-28T20:16:09.573Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nicolekrystyn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe for a salty/sweet party we had at work. It was a really simple recipe and so easy and quick to make! I ended up melting the butter and marshmallow fluff in the microwave in a big pyrex bowl, then stirred in the crunched up fritos. I put that all in an 8x8 pan and pressed down with parchment paper. I left them loosely covered with foil overnight and everybody loved them the next day at work! I'll definitely be making these again.",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-14T19:04:22.473Z"
          }
        ],
